FAST-GATK Mutect2 sample metadata boundary evidence (2026-08-31)

Latest regression closure:
  After preserving mate coordinates while aggregating repeated -I shards, the
  shared overlap-quality stage briefly changed Mutect2 conflicting-mate bases
  to zero.  GATK Mutect2 calls cleanOverlappingReadPairs with
  setConflictingToZero=false; the native shared caller now selects that mode
  for somatic_mode and keeps conflict telemetry without changing qualities.
  The pinned chr17 broad oracle is restored to an exact 6/6 site set on both
  OpenMP and Serial backends (GT 6/6, DP 5/6, AD 5/6; shared TLOD max absolute
  delta 3.500717, mean 0.743978; bit-identical=false).

Scope:
  Match GATK 4.6.2.0 when tumor input has no @RG SM sample metadata.

Oracle reproduction:
  A 40-base synthetic FASTA/SAM with @RG lines removed was run through:
    third_party/jdk17/bin/java -jar third_party/gatk-package/gatk-4.6.2.0/gatk-package-4.6.2.0-local.jar Mutect2 ...
  GATK exits non-zero during engine initialization with:
    java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: samples cannot be empty

Native implementation:
  fastgatk-native/src/mutect2_tool.cpp now probes the tumor header before
  aggregate decoding and before indexed --stream-by-region metadata setup.
  Empty HeaderSummary.samples raises:
    BAD_INPUT: tumor input header has no @RG SM sample (GATK requires a sample)
  This prevents all reads from being mixed and labeled with synthetic TUMOR.

Verification:
  FASTGATK_MUTECT2_BINARY=build/fastgatk-mutect2 python3 scripts/verify_mutect2.py
    PASS (default first @RG/SM, explicit missing sample, no-sample native + Java oracle,
    synthetic multi-ALT, streaming, sidecars and read-filter contracts)
  FASTGATK_MUTECT2_BINARY=build-serial/fastgatk-mutect2 FASTGATK_SERIAL=1 python3 scripts/verify_mutect2.py
    PASS (same contract on Serial backend)
  FASTGATK_MUTECT2_BINARY=build/fastgatk-mutect2 FASTGATK_REQUIRE_GATK_ORACLE=1 \
    python3 scripts/verify_mutect2_gatk_oracle.py
    PASS: GATK/native site set 6/6, GT 6/6, DP 5/6, AD 5/6, F1R2 archive member count exact;
    posterior remains non-bit-identical by design (max shared TLOD delta 5.908758).
  FASTGATK_MUTECT2_BINARY=build-serial/fastgatk-mutect2 FASTGATK_SERIAL=1 FASTGATK_REQUIRE_GATK_ORACLE=1 \
    python3 scripts/verify_mutect2_gatk_oracle.py
    PASS with the same semantic counts.
  The same verifier now constructs one multi-sample SAM and invokes native with
    -I combined-samples.sam --tumor-sample TUMOR --normal-sample NORMAL
    (no --normal-input alias).
    PASS: tumor_reads=40, normal_reads=8, VCF columns TUMOR/NORMAL, manifest
    tumor_normal=true and sample_name_filtering=true on both backends.
  It also repeats -I with a renamed second tumor shard and checks a mismatched
  sequence dictionary:
    PASS: two shards produce tumor_reads=80; incompatible @SQ length fails
    before decode with the explicit incompatible-sequence-dictionary error.
  A paired shard invocation (`-I tumor.sam -I normal.sam` with both sample
  selectors) also passes with tumor_reads=40 and normal_reads=8.  
  Aggregate repeated -I now applies the same stable coordinate merge used by
  region streaming (argv order is the tie-break), so overlap/fragment stages
  see GATK-like sorted input across shard boundaries.
  The stream contract additionally exercises a single indexed BAM with both
  `--tumor-sample` and `--normal-sample` (no `--normal-input`); the VCF header
  carries both selected sample columns, covering the same-file streaming
  branch.
  Repeated indexed `-I` is now accepted by `--stream-by-region`: each bounded
  core/halo tile validates all shard indexes and uses a stable coordinate merge.
  Duplicated indexed fixture shards produce exactly 2x the single-shard
  filtered read count and remain coordinate ordered with no duplicate loci.
  ctest --test-dir build -R fastgatk-mutect2-contract --output-on-failure
    1/1 passed in 9.63 s.
  ctest --test-dir build-serial -R fastgatk-mutect2-contract --output-on-failure
    1/1 passed in 10.28 s.
  The same verifier now runs GATK's common --sites-only-vcf-output true on
  the two-sample input.  Both OpenMP and Serial outputs preserve the tumor
  read/evidence counts and site INFO, emit an 8-column #CHROM header/body,
  retain BGZF/Tabix plus F1R2/stats, and record sites_only_vcf_output=true in
  stats and OutputManifest.
  The pinned GATK 4.6.2.0 oracle verifier also runs Java and native site-only
  commands: both accept the boolean, Java/native headers have no sample list,
  native site keys equal its ordinary VCF, and every emitted record has eight
  columns on both backends.

  The same synthetic contract now repeats --normal-sample NORMAL and
  --normal-sample OTHER_NORMAL on a single multi-sample input.  PASS on both
  OpenMP and Serial: aggregate normal_reads=12, stats and manifest expose
  normal_samples=[NORMAL,OTHER_NORMAL], and the VCF header/body carries
  TUMOR/NORMAL/OTHER_NORMAL with one independent FORMAT payload per normal.
  Somatic inference still consumes the deterministic aggregate normal evidence;
  release-specific joint normal posterior calibration remains explicit fallback.

Compatibility boundary:
  Tumor sample selection, no-sample failure mode, output indexing and sidecars
  are covered. Release-specific somatic priors/posterior calibration,
  complete FilterMutectCalls and whole-tool bit identity remain prototype/
  explicit Java fallback.

2026-08-31 output-index switch contract:
  `--create-output-variant-index false` was exercised on the combined
  tumor/normal fixture in both OpenMP and Serial builds.  The compressed VCF
  and all caller/posterior/F1R2/stats records remain complete and unchanged;
  the sibling `.tbi` is intentionally absent.  Stats and OutputManifest record
  `create_output_variant_index=false` and `vcf_index=false`.  The Mutect2
  verifier and targeted CTest passed on both backends, and the dispatcher
  registry contract now accepts the optional-boolean spelling.  This boundary
  also exercises enabled indexing for an uncompressed VCF: native writes a
  Tribble LinearIndex v3 sibling `.idx` (and no `.tbi`), and bundled GATK
  SelectVariants reads that index for a chr1 interval query.  This closes the
  prior uncompressed-output index gap for ordinary VCF text.
